    <h2>One Port, Many Possibilities</h2>

    <p>An open port only confirms that something is listening on that number. It does not tell you what that something actually is. Port 80 is commonly associated with web servers, but the exact software behind it could be Apache, Nginx, IIS, or something else entirely, each with its own set of known weaknesses.</p>

    <p>Service and version detection is the process of identifying the exact application and version number running behind an open port. Think of it like knowing a light is switched on in a house versus knowing the exact brand, model, and age of the lamp plugged in. The second gives you far more to work with.</p>

