<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Banner Grabbing</h2>

    <p>A banner is the text a service sends back the moment you connect to it. Many services announce themselves directly, revealing their name and version number without being asked. Reading these banners is the most direct way to identify what is running.</p>

    <p>Banner grabbing is the manual technique of connecting to a port and reading whatever response comes back, often using simple tools like netcat or telnet. It requires no special software, only a connection and a careful eye.</p>

    <table class="content-table">
        <thead>
