    <h2>Reading Results and Assessing Risk</h2>

    <p>Nmap output for a version scan lists four key columns: PORT, STATE, SERVICE, and VERSION. The first three tell you what is open and what kind of service it is, but the VERSION column is where the real risk assessment begins.</p>

    <p>An old, unmaintained version of a service can carry vulnerabilities that were patched years ago in newer releases. Comparing the detected version against known safe and unsafe versions is often the fastest way to prioritize what to investigate first.</p>

    <table class="content-table">
        <thead>
